15. Important backend concepts to revise
Concept	What you should understand
ORM	Maps Python objects to database tables
SQLAlchemy Session	Manages database operations and transactions
Pydantic	Validates incoming and outgoing data
Dependency Injection	Provides shared resources such as database sessions
JWT	Signed token used to authenticate requests
Password Hashing	Stores password hashes instead of plaintext passwords
HTTP 401	Authentication is missing or invalid
HTTP 403	User is authenticated but not permitted
HTTP 404	Requested resource does not exist
HTTP 409	Request conflicts with existing data
HTTP 422	Request validation failed
Pagination	Retrieves data in manageable pages
Database Relationship	Connects users and their AI requests
Production security reminders:
•	Use HTTPS in production.
•	Keep JWT secrets outside source control.
•	Use short-lived access tokens and consider refresh-token rotation.
•	Add rate limiting to login and registration.
•	Enforce user-level authorization on every private resource.
•	Use Alembic migrations rather than relying on create_all() for schema changes.
•	Avoid exposing internal exception messages or sensitive information.
