17. Week 2 mock interview – sample answers
Q1. Explain the architecture of your AI Platform Gateway.
My application uses FastAPI for REST API development, Pydantic for request validation, SQLAlchemy as the ORM and PostgreSQL for persistent storage. I separated API routes, business services, schemas, database models and configuration into independent modules. I also implemented JWT authentication to protect user-specific resources.
Q2. How does JWT authentication work in your application?
When a user logs in, the backend verifies their password against the stored Argon2 hash. If valid, it generates a signed JWT containing the user's ID and expiration time. The client sends that token in the Authorization header. FastAPI verifies the signature and expiration before allowing access to protected endpoints.
Q3. How would you scale this backend for multiple AI models?
I would separate model-provider integrations into independent adapter services, introduce a model registry, use asynchronous request handling where appropriate, add Redis for caching and rate limiting, and use background workers for long-running tasks. I would also introduce centralized logging, metrics, tracing and usage-based quotas.
